{"title": "Valve Index", "parts": {"header": "<div class=sd><div class=sd-grid><div class=sd-head><a class=sd-maker href=\"https://www.valvesoftware.com/\">Valve</a><h1 id=\"_top\">Valve Index</h1><p class=sd-type>VR headset with a global-shutter fisheye stereo pair and a 1 kHz IMU</p><p class=sd-chips><span class=\"cl cam unk\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"1.5\" y=\"4\" width=\"13\" height=\"9\" rx=\"2\"/><circle cx=\"8\" cy=\"8.5\" r=\"2.6\"/><path d=\"M5.5 4l1-1.6h3l1 1.6\"/></svg><span class=t>Camera not known <span class=x>×2</span></span></span><span class=\"cl imu\" title=\"iFixit chip ID\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><rect x=\"4\" y=\"4\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" rx=\"1.2\"/><path d=\"M6.5 4V2M9.5 4V2M6.5 14v-2M9.5 14v-2M4 6.5H2M4 9.5H2M14 6.5h-2M14 9.5h-2\"/></svg><span class=t><b>TDK InvenSense</b> <span class=p>ICM-20602</span></span> <a class=cl-src href=\"https://www.ifixit.com/Guide/Valve+Index+Chip+ID/155948\">Teardown</a></span></p></div><figure class=sd-plate><div class=sd-frame><img src=\"/media/sensors/valve-index/valve-index.jpg\" alt=\"Valve Index headset\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\"></div><figcaption><a href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1059530/\">Image: Valve, Steam store page</a></figcaption></figure><div class=sd-cta><div class=sd-buttons><a class=\"sd-btn primary\" href=\"https://store.steampowered.com/app/1059530/\">Valve product page</a><a class=sd-btn href=\"#specifications\">All specs (7)</a></div></div><div class=sd-specs><dl class=sd-rows><div class=sd-row><dt>Cameras</dt><dd>2 × 960×960, 54 Hz, grayscale<span class=sd-tag>Dataset</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Shutter</dt><dd>Global<span class=sd-tag>Dataset</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Field of view</dt><dd>Calibrated 120° × 120°<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Baseline</dt><dd>133.7 mm<span class=sd-tag>Measured</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>IMU</dt><dd>6-axis, about 1 kHz<span class=sd-tag>Dataset</span></dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Output</dt><dd>EuRoC layout, in the dataset<span class=sd-tag>Dataset</span></dd></div></dl><p class=sd-foot>Values from the Monado SLAM Datasets · 1 recording shown · CC BY 4.0 data</p></div></div></div>", "glance": "<p>VR headset from Valve with a front global-shutter fisheye stereo pair and a 6-axis IMU at about 1 kHz, solved from the Monado SLAM calibration data.</p><div class=band><figure class=demo><video src=\"/media/hero/hero_mic_960.mp4\" poster=\"/media/hero/hero_mic_960.jpg\" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload=metadata></video><figcaption>Recovered by MVIS from the Monado calibration data.</figcaption></figure><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.19<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0–cam1 baseline</span><b>133.7<small> mm</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>−0.04<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>140.1<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div><p class=sd-note>Reprojection is how far, in pixels, the detected corners lie from where the solve puts them. td is the camera–IMU time offset, and the lever arm is the camera–IMU position offset.</p><p class=sd-note>One recording shown, with no independent reference on this page. These values show what MVIS solved, not how close they are to the truth.</p>", "process": "<p>The path of the rig around the board, as MVIS solved it. To explore it:</p><ul class=list><li>Press <b>Play</b> or drag the bar to follow the path.</li><li>Use the <b>view buttons</b> to change the view.</li><li>Pick a <b>camera card</b> to put that camera on the frustum, the pyramid that shows its view.</li></ul><p>Each card draws the board from the solved pose, with the corners MVIS detected. We publish no camera images.</p><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=proc-wrap><button type=button class=proc-open hidden><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 220\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><p